# Glassmorphism — Style Reference

> Optics at night: glass has no color of its own — it borrows, bends and softens the light behind it.

**Theme:** dark

Glassmorphism is optics, not a palette. Real glass is colourless: it takes colour from the content layer and stays neutral itself, which is exactly the rule Apple's Liquid Glass follows. The system has three parts. First, a deep night canvas with two or three large-radius light wells — glass needs something to blur. Second, panels built from 5% to 12% white with 40px to 60px of backdrop-blur and 180% saturation. Third, direction of light: a 1px white inner highlight on the top edge, a 1px dark inner edge along the bottom, and a deep outer shadow. All three together produce thickness. The only permitted color is champagne gold, reserved for the primary CTA and key figures.

## Colors

| Name | Value | Token | Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| Night Deep | `#060a13` | `--color-night-deep` | The deepest layer: full-screen backdrops and base sections. Glass only reads when it floats above this. |
| Night | `#0b1322` | `--color-night` | The default page ground, one step lighter than the deepest tone so adjacent sections separate without a second color band. |
| Night Steel | `#16233a` | `--color-night-steel` | Secondary panels and input beds, for the places that need one more level beneath the glass. |
| Moon Steel | `#33517a` | `--color-moon-steel` | Secondary text, chart contrast and dividers. The closest thing the night palette has to a structural line. |
| Moonlight | `#7c9cc4` | `--color-moonlight` | Highlighted text, icons and data points — bright enough to register without competing with the CTA. |
| Champagne | `#e4b863` | `--color-champagne` | The only accent in the system. Reserved for the primary CTA, key figures and the single most important link. |
| Glass Fill | `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` | `--color-glass-fill` | Panel fill. Always translucent and never above 15%, or it degrades into a solid block. |

## Typography

### Inter — The only face in the system. Hierarchy comes from weight (400/500/600) and size, never from a second family.

- **Substitute:** SF Pro Display, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif
- **Weights:** 400, 500, 600
- **Sizes:** 12, 14, 16, 24, 40, 64
- **Line height:** 1.05 (display), 1.15 (headings), 1.6 (body)
- **Letter spacing:** -0.02em on display, 0.14em on uppercase labels

### Type Scale

| Role | Family | Weight | Size | Line Height | Letter Spacing | Token |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| display | Inter | 600 | 64px | 1.05 | -0.02em | `--text-display` |
| heading | Inter | 600 | 40px | 1.15 | -0.01em | `--text-heading` |
| subheading | Inter | 500 | 24px | 1.3 | — | `--text-subheading` |
| body-lg | Inter | 400 | 16px | 1.6 | — | `--text-body-lg` |
| body | Inter | 400 | 14px | 1.6 | — | `--text-body` |
| label | Inter | 500 | 12px | 1.4 | 0.14em | `--text-label` |

## Spacing & Layout

**Base unit:** 8px
**Density:** comfortable

### Spacing Scale

| Name | Value | Token |
|---|---|---|
| 8 | 8px | `--spacing-8` |
| 16 | 16px | `--spacing-16` |
| 24 | 24px | `--spacing-24` |
| 32 | 32px | `--spacing-32` |
| 48 | 48px | `--spacing-48` |
| 64 | 64px | `--spacing-64` |
| 96 | 96px | `--spacing-96` |
| 128 | 128px | `--spacing-128` |

### Border Radius

| Element | Value |
|---|---|
| cards | 24px |
| panels | 32px |
| buttons | 16px |
| inputs | 14px |
| pills | 999px |

- **Page max-width:** 1280px
- **Section gap:** 128px
- **Card padding:** 32px
- **Element gap:** 16px

## Components

### Glass Panel

**Role:** Every content container: cards, panels, overlays

8% white fill, 40px backdrop-blur, 180% saturation, 1px white-at-15% border, 24px radius. The shadow is always three layers at once: an outer 0 16px 40px dark spread, a 1px white inset highlight on the top edge, and a 1px dark inset edge along the bottom. Padding 32px. On hover the fill rises to 14%, the border to 30%, the outer shadow to the 64px step and the panel lifts 2px, over 500ms with cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1).

- **Sizes:** padding 32px; radius 24px
- **States:** hover: fill 8% to 14%, border 15% to 30%, translateY -2px

### Champagne CTA

**Role:** Primary action; one per page

Champagne fill, deep-night text, fully rounded at 999px, no border. 16px type at weight 500, padding 14px 28px. On hover the fill goes to 92% opacity, the button lifts 1px and gains a 0 12px 32px glow at 25% champagne, over the same 500ms easing.

- **Sizes:** padding 14px 28px; radius 999px
- **States:** hover: lift 1px, glow; focus-visible: 2px champagne outline, 2px offset

### Glass Input

**Role:** Form input and search field

Transparent fill, 1px white-at-15% border, 14px radius, no outer shadow. Padding 12px 16px, 14px type, placeholder in moon steel. Focus raises the border to 40% and adds a 3px outer ring at 8% white without changing the box size.

- **States:** focus: border 40%, 3px outer ring

### Stat Tile

**Role:** Key figures and dashboard metrics

A lighter glass panel: 5% white fill, 24px blur, 16px radius, 24px padding. A 12px uppercase 0.14em label in moon steel sits above a 40px figure at weight 600 in white, with 8px of air below for the trend note. The figure takes champagne only if it is the single emphasis on the page.

### Night Nav

**Role:** Top navigation

72px tall, 4% white fill, 20px blur, border only along the bottom at 10% white. Wordmark at 16px weight 500 on the left, 14px moon-steel links in the middle that shift to moonlight on hover, one champagne CTA on the right. Past the first viewport the fill rises to 8%.

## Do's and Don'ts

### Do

- Light the background first: deep night ground plus two or three large-radius light wells
- Glass panels use 5% to 12% white and never exceed 15%
- Blur starts at 40px and always pairs with 180% saturation
- Shadows carry three layers: outer spread, white top inset highlight, dark bottom inset edge
- Champagne is the only accent, reserved for the CTA and key figures
- Radius starts at 16px; panels take 24px to 32px
- Transitions run 500ms on cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)

### Don't

- No purple-pink AI gradients such as #667eea, #764ba2 or #f093fb
- Do not place glass on a flat solid background; there is nothing to blur
- Never tint the glass itself — color belongs to the background
- No backdrop-blur-sm or any blur below 40px
- Do not omit backdrop-saturate
- No opaque fills such as bg-white or bg-black
- No square corners and no radius under 16px
- No single-layer flat shadow
- No 100ms to 150ms transitions; glass moves slowly

## Surfaces

| Level | Name | Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Night | `#0b1322` | 页面底，所有光斑画在它上面 |
| 1 | Glass | `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` | 标准玻璃面板 |
| 2 | Glass Raised | `rgba(255,255,255,0.14)` | hover 态与需要更靠前的浮层 |

## Elevation

- **Glass rest:** `0 16px 40px rgba(3,7,18,0.5), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.22), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(2,6,16,0.35)`
- **Glass hover:** `0 24px 64px rgba(3,7,18,0.6), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.32), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(2,6,16,0.35)`

## Imagery

There must be a light source. Use night photography, dark product shots, or two to three large-radius radial gradients drawn in CSS. Images stay low-saturation and dark with obvious highlight areas, because glass needs those highlights to read as refraction. No illustration, no icon walls, no flat solid backgrounds.

## Layout

Twelve columns capped at 1280px. Section rhythm 128px, panel padding 32px, 16px between elements. Content floats above the light wells, which stay pinned to the background layer and move with slight parallax. No more than three glass panels per viewport; past that there is no solid reference left and the material stops reading as glass.

## Agent Prompt Guide

### Implementation Contract

- Use the requested page, user task and real content as the brief. Implement only the requested scope; identify missing business information instead of inventing data or capabilities.
- Inspect the current project, stack and components first. Reuse its structure, routes, dependencies and components; do not rebuild unrelated pages or features.
- Use the project's breakpoints to adapt columns and spacing for narrow and desktop screens. Preserve hierarchy and prevent accidental horizontal overflow.
- For interactions in scope, support keyboard focus and reduced motion, with applicable disabled, loading, empty and error states.
- Run the project's existing checks after implementation. Report only tests and visual checks actually run, and list unverified behavior.

QUICK COLOR REFERENCE:

- text: `#ffffff`
- background: `#0b1322`
- muted: `#7c9cc4`
- accent: `#e4b863`
- glassFill: `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)`
- glassBorder: `rgba(255,255,255,0.15)`

EXAMPLE COMPONENT PROMPTS:

1. Build a glass panel: background rgba(255,255,255,0.08), backdrop-filter blur(40px) saturate(180%), 1px border rgba(255,255,255,0.15), 24px radius, 32px padding. The shadow is box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(3,7,18,0.5), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.22), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(2,6,16,0.35). The page ground is #0b1322 with two large radial light wells behind the panel (one #33517a, one #e4b863 at 0.25 opacity).
2. Build a night hero: left column starts with a 12px uppercase 0.14em label in #7c9cc4, then a 64px weight-600 headline in #ffffff at -0.02em tracking, then 16px body copy in #7c9cc4 at 1.6 line height, and a champagne pill button (#e4b863 fill, #060a13 text, 14px 28px padding) underneath. The right column holds a glass card whose 500ms hover raises the fill to 14% and lifts it 2px.

## Similar Brands

- **Apple** — Same optical principle: glass takes the background's color, stays neutral itself, and reads its thickness from a top-edge highlight
- **Linear** — Dark ground with a single accent, dividing space through panel levels rather than borders
- **Vercel** — Night-toned ground and restrained light; hierarchy from luminance rather than ornament

## Quick Start

```css

:root {
  /* Colors */
  --color-night-deep: #060a13;
  --color-night: #0b1322;
  --color-night-steel: #16233a;
  --color-moon-steel: #33517a;
  --color-moonlight: #7c9cc4;
  --color-champagne: #e4b863;
  --color-glass-fill: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);

  /* Typography — Font Families */
  --font-sans: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;

  /* Typography — Scale */
  --text-display: 64px;
  --leading-display: 1.05;
  --tracking-display: -0.02em;
  --text-heading: 40px;
  --leading-heading: 1.15;
  --tracking-heading: -0.01em;
  --text-subheading: 24px;
  --leading-subheading: 1.3;
  --text-body-lg: 16px;
  --leading-body-lg: 1.6;
  --text-body: 14px;
  --leading-body: 1.6;
  --text-label: 12px;
  --leading-label: 1.4;
  --tracking-label: 0.14em;

  /* Typography — Weights */
  --font-weight-regular: 400;
  --font-weight-medium: 500;
  --font-weight-semibold: 600;

  /* Spacing */
  --spacing-unit: 8px;
  --spacing-8: 8px;
  --spacing-16: 16px;
  --spacing-24: 24px;
  --spacing-32: 32px;
  --spacing-48: 48px;
  --spacing-64: 64px;
  --spacing-96: 96px;
  --spacing-128: 128px;

  /* Layout */
  --page-max-width: 1280px;
  --section-gap: 128px;
  --card-padding: 32px;
  --element-gap: 16px;
  --density: comfortable;

  /* Border Radius */
  --radius-cards: 24px;
  --radius-panels: 32px;
  --radius-buttons: 16px;
  --radius-inputs: 14px;
  --radius-pills: 999px;

  /* Surfaces */
  --surface-night: #0b1322;
  --surface-glass: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
  --surface-glass-raised: rgba(255,255,255,0.14);
}

```

